Windows Vista, it seems, doesn't support full-screen text mode.  Pressing
Alt-Enter gives an error box.  (An MS-DOS program that tries to use graphics is
terminated at the attempt to do so.)

I know that some players prefer text to tiles.  The graphical front end for
Windows can show a text map; but would it be worthwhile to create a "pseudo-tty"
port that would operate as a windowed program, but duplicate the look of the
traditional text-mode interface?

Such a port need not be limited to Windows, of course.

